WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.100
For shows as dark and suspenseful as NCIS,
it's hard to imagine one scene's subject matter

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.990
seeming harder to watch than the rest.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.450
So what event could be so heart wrenching
that it outshines an entire season?

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.809
Keep watching to discover the one scene NCIS
Season 9 took too far!

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:19.450
As sad as it is to see familiar faces leave,
one universal truth has emerged: NCIS likes

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.050
to craft dramatic exits for its characters.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.430
As time has gone on, audiences have gotten
used to living with the worry that something

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.650
terrible could happen to their favorite investigator
at any moment.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.820
Packed with ups, downs, major plot twists,
and plenty of NCIS's classic brand of drama,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.400
Season 9 is no exception to this gruesome
storytelling style.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.680
In it, we see everything from Tony DiNozzo,
played by Michael Weatherly, getting shot,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.570
to Cote de Pablo's character Ziva David receiving
a marriage proposal.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.190
In crime dramas like NCIS, there are plenty
of scenes that may be difficult for some audiences

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.431
to watch, especially while experiencing the
rest of the emotional turmoil included in

00:00:53.431 --> 00:00:54.431
Season 9.

00:00:54.431 --> 00:00:58.800
However, there is one particular scene involving
a major character that is almost too shocking

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.800
to talk about.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.989
In NCIS Season 9 Episode 24, Till Death Do
Us Part, it's not a grisly crime scene or

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:07.340
awkward moment that leaves viewers reeling.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.140
Instead, audiences get a taste of this show's
trademark heartbreak when, at the end of this

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:15.479
action-packed season finale, fan-favorite
medical examiner Donald "Ducky" Mallard, played

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:17.350
by David McCallum, has a heart attack.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:22.040
The shocking event is one of many packed into
the hour-long season finale, and its placement

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.680
in the latter half of the episode only adds
to the tension.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.530
Till Death Do Us Part sees Gibbs and his team
pull out all the stops as they continue to

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.950
investigate a series of deadly explosions.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.619
Gibbs recruits Dr. Samantha Ryan, portrayed
by guest star Jamie Lee Curtis, to help identify

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:36.619
the cause.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:40.950
Soon, a man named Harper Dearing, played by
Richard Schiff, becomes the focus of the NCIS

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.180
team's investigation.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.140
In the final act, Dearing's last bomb goes
off right outside NCIS headquarters.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.020
This scene would be dramatic enough by itself,
but it's only made worse by the fact that

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.690
Gibbs, McGee, Ziva, DiNozzo, and Abby are
all trapped inside by the damage.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.840
In the episode's final scene, Ducky is seen
walking along the beach.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.860
As he takes in the view, he receives a call,
presumably about the fatal bombing.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.040
Ducky demands that nobody touches the bodies
of the deceased, then pauses as a heart attack

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.040
strikes.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:14.540
"It's imperative that no one touches the deceased
until I…Until I re-"

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.700
The last image of the Season 9 finale shows
Ducky collapsed on the beach as the tide rolls

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.700
in.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.720
The heart attack seems to be the result of
overwhelming stress from the shocking phone

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.599
call, and audiences are left to wonder about
Ducky's fate, and the fates of all his trapped

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:27.599
team members.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:31.930
The NCIS Season 9 finale ends so dramatically,
the fact that it has stuck in the minds of

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.739
fans almost a decade after it aired should
come as no great surprise.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:40.629
In June 2021, when a Reddit user posed the
question, "Any episodes of NCIS that made

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:41.629
you cry?"

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:44.829
fans had no trouble coming up with plenty
of iconic moments that hit a little too close

00:02:44.829 --> 00:02:45.829
to home.

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:49.650
Even still, Ducky's heart attack made many
viewers' lists despite the 18 seasons of drama

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.849
they had to pick from when the thread was
posted.

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:55.760
A redditor included this scene in their top
three, along with the deaths of Gibbs' father

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.849
and Palmer's wife.

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:58.269
The commenter went on to clarify,

00:02:58.269 --> 00:03:01.760
"There are more that hug at the heart, but
these three made me cry."

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.189
Ducky is a vital character in the series,
whose charm and random educational banter

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:07.010
has fans fully invested in his well-being.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:11.599
So watching him have a heart attack in the
ninth season finale of NCIS was a scene that

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:15.200
was a bit too much for some audience members
to handle.

